{"source": "https://ioffice.jbnu.ac.kr/ioffice/22297/subview.do", "title": "The Feeling Korea", "text": "k2web/com/cop/site/layout.jsp ioffice_JW_MS_K2WT001_S ■ Introduction This program not only provides an excellent education in the Korean language taught by excellent teachers but also takes full advantage of the excellent variety of local Korean cultural opportunities and experiences, such as Taekwondo and, traditional music. This is accomplished through interactions between students and volunteers who are responsible for interpreting and guiding foreign participants in order to increase mutual understanding of two cultures, making it possible to create a global mindset. Participants can experience the essence of both traditional and modern Korea as well various Korean cultural activities in a short period of time. ■ Period of the Program The program is held 1-2 times during each Summer / Winter vacation for two weeks. - Period: 2 weeks - Schedule · Morning: Korean Language Class for Foreigners · Afternoon: Korean Traditional Cultural Activities ■ Subject and Credits - Subject: Introduction to Korean Culture - Credits: 3(45hours) for 2 weeks ■ Participation Fee Contents Non-Sister Universities Sister Universities Mandatory Fees Including: Accommodation, Meals, Tuition, Field Trip,"}
