{"source": "https://ioffice.jbnu.ac.kr/bbs/ioffice/3549/362466/artclView.do", "title": "[For students entering Korea with a new visa issued by the embassy] Application for Alien Registration", "text": "K2Web Wizard Created 2025.07.07 Modified 2025.07.07 Writer 국제협력부 Views 98 [For students entering Korea with a new visa issued by the embassy] Application for Alien Registration Alien Registration (35,000 KRW): For those applying for a new Alien Registration Card (ARC) [Processing time: 4 to 8 weeks] ○ Required Documents 1. Application form 2. Passport (copy) 3. Standard-sized photo (white background) 4. Certificate of tuition payment 5. Certificate of admission (standard format) 6. Certificate of enrollment (after semester begins) 7. Proof of residence (one of the following: official mail from a government office, rental contract, notification of stay expiration, utility bill receipt, or dormitory move-in confirmation). ※ If you are not living in a house directly under your name (e.g., staying at a friend’s place), you must submit a Residence/Accommodation Confirmation Form along with a copy of the provider's ID. 8. Fingerprint registration (After submitting your application, you must visit the immigration office on the scheduled date to complete fingerprinting in order to finalize the alien registration process.) Attachments ★통합신청서(신고서)_전북대학교.hwp 거주숙소제공사실확인서(영문병기).hwp"}
